WEBVTT

00:00:14.639 --> 00:00:17.350
♪ ♪

00:00:34.325 --> 00:00:37.120
♪ ♪

00:00:45.962 --> 00:00:48.631
WONKA:
Dear people of the world,

00:00:48.715 --> 00:00:50.466
I, Willy Wonka,

00:00:50.508 --> 00:00:53.720
have decided to allow
five children to visit

00:00:53.803 --> 00:00:55.179
my factory this year.

00:00:55.263 --> 00:00:57.098
In addition,
one of these children

00:00:57.140 --> 00:00:58.641
shall receive a special prize

00:00:58.683 --> 00:01:02.186
beyond anything
you could ever imagine.

00:01:02.270 --> 00:01:04.314
MAN:
Five golden tickets

00:01:04.355 --> 00:01:07.150
have been hidden underneath
the ordinary wrapping paper

00:01:07.191 --> 00:01:08.651
of five ordinary Wonka bars.

00:01:08.735 --> 00:01:11.529
These five candy bars
may be anywhere, in any shop,

00:01:11.613 --> 00:01:16.492
in any street, in any town
in any country in the world.

00:01:16.534 --> 00:01:17.577
( buzzer sounds )

00:01:17.660 --> 00:01:20.455
( talking excitedly )

00:01:26.252 --> 00:01:29.672
( crowd clamoring )

00:01:34.719 --> 00:01:36.512
( goat bleating )

00:01:40.850 --> 00:01:45.188
( chattering excitedly )

00:01:50.360 --> 00:01:52.153
GRANDPA JOE:
Wouldn’t it be something,

00:01:52.195 --> 00:01:55.698
Charlie, to open a bar
of candy and find

00:01:55.740 --> 00:01:57.659
a golden ticket inside?

00:01:57.700 --> 00:01:58.826
I know.

00:01:58.868 --> 00:02:00.703
But I only get one bar a year--

00:02:00.745 --> 00:02:01.871
for my birthday.

00:02:01.955 --> 00:02:04.332
Well, it’s your birthday
next week.

00:02:04.374 --> 00:02:07.835
You have as much chance
as anybody does.

00:02:07.877 --> 00:02:09.170
Balderdash.

00:02:09.212 --> 00:02:11.130
The kids who are going
to find the golden tickets

00:02:11.214 --> 00:02:13.299
are the ones who can afford
to buy candy bars every day.

00:02:13.383 --> 00:02:16.219
Our Charlie gets
only one a year.

00:02:16.260 --> 00:02:17.303
He doesn’t have a chance.

00:02:17.387 --> 00:02:19.639
GRANDMA JOSEPHINE:
Everyone

00:02:19.722 --> 00:02:21.057
has a chance, Charlie.

00:02:21.099 --> 00:02:22.558
Mark my words.

00:02:22.642 --> 00:02:27.897
The kid who finds the first
ticket will be fat, fat, fat.

00:02:27.939 --> 00:02:28.940
( shutters clicking )

00:02:29.023 --> 00:02:30.233
This way.
Augustus!

00:02:35.738 --> 00:02:38.533
I eating the Wonka bar
and I taste something

00:02:38.574 --> 00:02:40.576
that is not chocolate.

00:02:40.618 --> 00:02:43.705
Or coconut...

00:02:43.746 --> 00:02:46.416
or walnut, or peanut butter,

00:02:46.457 --> 00:02:48.793
or nougat,

00:02:48.876 --> 00:02:51.004
or butter brittle or caramel,

00:02:51.087 --> 00:02:53.006
or sprinkles.

00:02:53.089 --> 00:02:57.051
So I look and...

00:02:58.052 --> 00:02:59.762
I find ze golden ticket.

00:02:59.846 --> 00:03:01.973
Augustus, how did you celebrate?

00:03:02.056 --> 00:03:05.268
I eat more candy.

00:03:08.062 --> 00:03:11.107
We knew Augustus would find
the golden ticket.

00:03:11.190 --> 00:03:14.944
He eats so many candy
bars a day that it was

00:03:15.028 --> 00:03:17.780
not possible for him
not to find one.

00:03:17.822 --> 00:03:20.950
( reporters clamoring )

00:03:20.992 --> 00:03:23.786
NEWSCASTER:
...ticket claimed
and only four more...

00:03:23.828 --> 00:03:25.246
Told you it’d be a porker.

00:03:25.288 --> 00:03:27.832
What a repulsive boy.

00:03:27.915 --> 00:03:29.500
Only four golden tickets left.

00:03:29.584 --> 00:03:34.422
Now that they found one,
things will really get crazy.

00:03:34.464 --> 00:03:36.799
NEWSCASTER:
...of every shape, size and hue.

00:03:39.886 --> 00:03:40.887
REPORTER:
Veruca?

00:03:40.970 --> 00:03:42.013
Can you spell that
for us please?

00:03:42.096 --> 00:03:45.433
GIRL:
V-E-R-U-C-A.

00:03:45.475 --> 00:03:47.226
Veruca Salt.

00:03:48.352 --> 00:03:50.146
As soon as my little
Veruca told me

00:03:50.188 --> 00:03:52.231
she had to have one
of these golden tickets,

00:03:52.315 --> 00:03:53.483
I started buying up

00:03:53.524 --> 00:03:55.735
all the Wonka bars
I could lay my hands on.

00:03:55.818 --> 00:03:57.028
Thousands of them.

00:03:57.111 --> 00:03:58.529
Hundreds of thousands.

00:03:58.613 --> 00:04:00.907
I’m in the nut business,
you see.

00:04:00.990 --> 00:04:02.784
So I say to my workers...

00:04:02.825 --> 00:04:04.243
Morning, ladies.

00:04:04.327 --> 00:04:05.828
From now on,
you can stop shelling peanuts

00:04:05.912 --> 00:04:07.830
and start shelling the wrappers

00:04:07.872 --> 00:04:10.166
off these chocolate bars
instead.

00:04:10.208 --> 00:04:12.335
( alarm blares,
machinery clanks )

00:04:23.638 --> 00:04:26.265
MR. SALT:
Three days went by
and we had no luck.

00:04:26.349 --> 00:04:27.767
It was terrible.

00:04:27.850 --> 00:04:30.353
My little Veruca got more
and more upset each day.

00:04:30.394 --> 00:04:31.938
Where’s my
golden ticket?

00:04:32.021 --> 00:04:34.690
I want my golden ticket.

00:04:36.651 --> 00:04:38.027
Well, gentlemen,
I just hated to see

00:04:38.111 --> 00:04:39.403
my little girl
feeling unhappy like that.

00:04:39.487 --> 00:04:41.239
I vowed I would
keep up the search

00:04:41.322 --> 00:04:43.282
until I could give her
what she wanted.

00:04:43.366 --> 00:04:45.701
Then finally...

00:04:45.743 --> 00:04:48.204
I found her a ticket.

00:04:48.287 --> 00:04:50.706
( paper ripping )

00:04:54.502 --> 00:04:57.296
( paper rustling )

00:05:04.053 --> 00:05:07.849
♪ ♪

00:05:14.438 --> 00:05:17.984
Daddy, I want another pony.

00:05:18.067 --> 00:05:19.652
( reporters clamoring on TV )

00:05:19.735 --> 00:05:21.737
She’s even worse
than the fat boy.

00:05:21.779 --> 00:05:23.614
I didn’t think
that was really fair.

00:05:23.698 --> 00:05:26.033
She didn’t find
the ticket herself.

00:05:26.075 --> 00:05:28.244
Don’t worry about it, Charlie.

00:05:28.327 --> 00:05:30.413
That man spoils his daughter,

00:05:30.496 --> 00:05:32.582
and no good ever comes

00:05:32.623 --> 00:05:35.293
from spoiling a child
like that.

00:05:38.838 --> 00:05:42.717
Charlie, Mum and I thought

00:05:42.758 --> 00:05:46.679
maybe you want to open
your birthday present tonight.

00:05:49.932 --> 00:05:52.018
( turns off TV )

00:05:52.101 --> 00:05:53.936
Here you are.

